          "heading": "WRU publishes Keystone report data justifying future professional team cuts",
          "body": "The Welsh Rugby Union has released the independent Keystone report, the 68-page document central to the governing body’s plan to reduce the number of professional men’s sides from four to three by 2028. The data outlines the methodology behind the board’s decision to prioritise licences for Cardiff and Dragons in the east. This follows sustained criticism from fans and stakeholders in west Wales, where Ospreys and Scarlets remain locked in an ongoing struggle to retain their professional status."
        },
